      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep existing-hex selection available during name edits**\n\nWhen either name field has unsaved changes, this guard also blocks selecting existing hexes: `mapHexClickRef.current` calls `mutationBlocked()` before distinguishing candidate generation from ordinary `setSelectedHex` navigation. I reproduced that clicking another existing hex leaves the selection unchanged until the draft is cancelled. This prevents inspecting other regions, POIs, or notes while composing a name, contrary to the documented availability of navigation during edits. Apply the dirty-name restriction to document-changing actions while allowing existing-hex selection.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
